(7246669, 1121242, 30049, '<td valign="top">Lovely image.  Really like the color and the timing to catch the birds coming thru.  One nit ... the horizon appears to be tilted to the left.</td>', 'Lovely image.  Really like the color and the timing to catch the birds coming thru.  One nit ... the horizon appears to be tilted to the left.', '2014-08-02 11:34:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7246670, 1124726, 30049, '<td valign="top">A fair amount of shadow recovery seems to be applied as her neck and check are very grainy/noisy in comparison to the other parts of the photo.  I also wonder about the placement of her hand ... with the hard dark line meeting the hand in that area it really jumps out which emphasizes the awkward angle.</td>', 'A fair amount of shadow recovery seems to be applied as her neck and check are very grainy/noisy in comparison to the other parts of the photo.  I also wonder about the placement of her hand ... with the hard dark line meeting the hand in that area it really jumps out which emphasizes the awkward angle.', '2014-08-02 11:37:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7246671, 1122550, 30049, '<td valign="top">It''s ok I guess, but quite frankly the photo is missing a strong subject IMO.  Everything is soft and nothing of high interest is in solid focus.  Sorry.</td>', 'It''s ok I guess, but quite frankly the photo is missing a strong subject IMO.  Everything is soft and nothing of high interest is in solid focus.  Sorry.', '2014-08-02 11:38:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7246672, 1123528, 30049, '<td valign="top">Lovely fellow.  :-)  Could have gone with a tad less negative space up top IMO.  The main subject here is the "eyes" and hairy-ness of the spider ... that is lost a little bit with the small area of the photo dedicated to it (i.e. a tighter crop may be better here?).  Also, the highlights are blown on the spiders back (that area is nearly the same size as the "subject" matter).</td>', 'Lovely fellow.  :-)  Could have gone with a tad less negative space up top IMO.  The main subject here is the "eyes" and hairy-ness of the spider ... that is lost a little bit with the small area of the photo dedicated to it (i.e. a tighter crop may be better here?).  Also, the highlights are blown on the spiders back (that area is nearly the same size as the "subject" matter).', '2014-08-02 11:43:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7246673, 1125721, 30049, '<td valign="top">Cool to catch having a moose in your yard.  Fun subject for sure.  Could be a little warmer (color tone) and a bit sharper (looks like a fair amount of zoom factor in here?).</td>', 'Cool to catch having a moose in your yard.  Fun subject for sure.  Could be a little warmer (color tone) and a bit sharper (looks like a fair amount of zoom factor in here?).', '2014-08-02 11:45:49.000000', NULL, 1),
