(7248926, 1125813, 77188, '<td valign="top">Yes, I agree that the focus is in the wrong place.  Since I took this photo when travelling I had no option to go back and take another shot with the right bits in focus though.  The reason I picked the photo for the Free Study is that I love how the colours turned out.  I normally never edit my photos (this image is only slightly cropped), meaning that if the colours don''t look nice right out of the camera I don''t use the photo.<br/> <br/>Now, in arrears I should probably take more photos of the same object, to ensure that at least one of them ends up with correct focus :)<br/> <br/>Anyway, thanks for the feedback!</td>', 'Yes, I agree that the focus is in the wrong place.  Since I took this photo when travelling I had no option to go back and take another shot with the right bits in focus though.  The reason I picked the photo for the Free Study is that I love how the colours turned out.  I normally never edit my photos (this image is only slightly cropped), meaning that if the colours don''t look nice right out of the camera I don''t use the photo. Now, in arrears I should probably take more photos of the same object, to ensure that at least one of them ends up with correct focus :) Anyway, thanks for the feedback!', '2014-08-08 09:07:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248935, 1125689, 117474, '<td valign="top">This is a phenomenal image!</td>', 'This is a phenomenal image!', '2014-08-08 09:27:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248936, 1125507, 19944, '<td valign="top">I gave you a rounded up six.  I think it may not have done so well because the actual water fall take up such a small portion of the photo.  Also, the light &amp; contrast is uneven, very light and low contrast at the top, darker and nice contrast at the bottom.  I much prefer the landscape version you posted. That, too probably would have gotten a six from me, but it would have been a rounded down six.</td>', 'I gave you a rounded up six.  I think it may not have done so well because the actual water fall take up such a small portion of the photo.  Also, the light & contrast is uneven, very light and low contrast at the top, darker and nice contrast at the bottom.  I much prefer the landscape version you posted. That, too probably would have gotten a six from me, but it would have been a rounded down six.', '2014-08-08 09:28:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248937, 1125507, 96574, '<td valign="top">It''s a nice scene Joshua but I think the picture overall is too busy.  My eye is in constant movement and can''t really land on a focal point.  I think the top portion could''ve been cropped out (the area of trees) and that may have given more focus on the foremost water fall area.  The contrast seems a bit to strong on the image overall as well.<br/> <br/>Looking at your other shot in landscape orientation, I definitely like that one better.  It looks like you added a stronger vignette in that my attention goes directly to the waterfall.<br/> <br/>Just one voters opinion so hope this helps.</td>', 'It''s a nice scene Joshua but I think the picture overall is too busy.  My eye is in constant movement and can''t really land on a focal point.  I think the top portion could''ve been cropped out (the area of trees) and that may have given more focus on the foremost water fall area.  The contrast seems a bit to strong on the image overall as well. Looking at your other shot in landscape orientation, I definitely like that one better.  It looks like you added a stronger vignette in that my attention goes directly to the waterfall. Just one voters opinion so hope this helps.', '2014-08-08 09:29:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248944, 1121979, 163081, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mariuca:</b></div><hr/><i> I keep coming back to it (and bump) and have one thought that nags me: wouldn''t it be more powerful if you would crop the sky? I love the composition a lot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There is no sky on the picture, this is the sea on top. <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by mariuca: I keep coming back to it (and bump) and have one thought that nags me: wouldn''t it be more powerful if you would crop the sky? I love the composition a lot.   There is no sky on the picture, this is the sea on top. ', '2014-08-08 09:46:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248986, 1125689, 12611, '<td valign="top">amazing scene- congrats.</td>', 'amazing scene- congrats.', '2014-08-08 10:39:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248989, 1125811, 12611, '<td valign="top">excellent presentation on this, the viewer is fooled into thinking that the focus is on the man, when, in fact the only thought is "purple."</td>', 'excellent presentation on this, the viewer is fooled into thinking that the focus is on the man, when, in fact the only thought is "purple."', '2014-08-08 10:43:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248990, 1125842, 12611, '<td valign="top">A beautiful scene Allesandro-the wispy clouds appear cosmic...</td>', 'A beautiful scene Allesandro-the wispy clouds appear cosmic...', '2014-08-08 10:44:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248994, 1125507, 50695, '<td valign="top">I gave it a 5, which is really high for a waterfall shot. I like the wide angle distortion and the fogginess of the top contrasting with the sharpness of the bottom ... all stuff the other voters probably did not like.<br/> <br/>What Cuttooth says is "too busy" I would say is a good, dynamic rhythm that keeps the eye moving. But DPC is LCD. Keep it simple.</td>', 'I gave it a 5, which is really high for a waterfall shot. I like the wide angle distortion and the fogginess of the top contrasting with the sharpness of the bottom ... all stuff the other voters probably did not like. What Cuttooth says is "too busy" I would say is a good, dynamic rhythm that keeps the eye moving. But DPC is LCD. Keep it simple.', '2014-08-08 10:49:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248995, 1125928, 12611, '<td valign="top">Not often is there such beautiful intensity in saturation without going to far... you achieved that warmth without pushing over the edge. I understand the angle, but perhaps this would have done even better if the fishing pole angle was out into the dark rather than forward, which appeared to be back at land, facing the sun. a bit of negative space into the dark with a leading fishing pole would have nailed it- even better than it already is, which is still terrific!</td>', 'Not often is there such beautiful intensity in saturation without going to far... you achieved that warmth without pushing over the edge. I understand the angle, but perhaps this would have done even better if the fishing pole angle was out into the dark rather than forward, which appeared to be back at land, facing the sun. a bit of negative space into the dark with a leading fishing pole would have nailed it- even better than it already is, which is still terrific!', '2014-08-08 10:50:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7248997, 1125384, 12611, '<td valign="top">Great action Susan.</td>', 'Great action Susan.', '2014-08-08 10:51:02.000000', NULL, 0),
