(7249018, 1125718, 12611, '<td valign="top">I like the geometrics set along side the concept of romantic love, each oblivious to each other, but connected in ways that can''t be expressed with words, a photo frame suffices...</td>', 'I like the geometrics set along side the concept of romantic love, each oblivious to each other, but connected in ways that can''t be expressed with words, a photo frame suffices...', '2014-08-08 10:57:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7249022, 1125807, 12611, '<td valign="top">I like the warm golden middle ground, and the overexposed sun. it captures that point of the day that does not show up as much on film, probably because the sun behind creates a flatness, a fuzziness- but this is the very best part of the shot. (Perhaps that leaning tree didn''t do you any favors with the voters...)</td>', 'I like the warm golden middle ground, and the overexposed sun. it captures that point of the day that does not show up as much on film, probably because the sun behind creates a flatness, a fuzziness- but this is the very best part of the shot. (Perhaps that leaning tree didn''t do you any favors with the voters...)', '2014-08-08 11:00:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7249030, 1125934, 12611, '<td valign="top">I like the way it almost seems like a Renaissance statue, with the male subject having impossibly big hands and a small head with a slightly weak chin and curly hair, reminiscnet of the boyishness of David...</td>', 'I like the way it almost seems like a Renaissance statue, with the male subject having impossibly big hands and a small head with a slightly weak chin and curly hair, reminiscnet of the boyishness of David...', '2014-08-08 11:05:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7249032, 1125291, 39184, '<td valign="top">Hi Arna, that is a great first entry!  I was disappointed to see that nobody has yet responded to your wish for feedback and tips.<br/> <br/>There is one step that would have rocketed this image to a much higher placement in this challenge:  A simple S-Curve curves adjustment to increase contrast.<br/> <br/>Check out the tutorials under "Learn" in the bar at the top of the page for a lot of good information.  The specific tutorial on curves adjustment is here:  //www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=58<br/> <br/>Try the second example on S-Curves for increase in contrast and keep entering challenges!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-08-08 10:20:03.</i></td>', 'Hi Arna, that is a great first entry!  I was disappointed to see that nobody has yet responded to your wish for feedback and tips. There is one step that would have rocketed this image to a much higher placement in this challenge:  A simple S-Curve curves adjustment to increase contrast. Check out the tutorials under "Learn" in the bar at the top of the page for a lot of good information.  The specific tutorial on curves adjustment is here:  //www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=58 Try the second example on S-Curves for increase in contrast and keep entering challenges!', '2014-08-08 11:19:44.000000', '2014-08-08 11:20:03.000000', 0),
(7249033, 1125507, 63218, '<td valign="top">For me it looks muddy &amp; the color black in the upper right dominates the image. IMO the best thing about a landscape is its abstract quality, &amp; this one doesn''t have much abstract-for me, the best thing about this is the rocks underwater. Next time you go out to get some nice landscapes, take a moment to get a few macro shots as well. But I am not a landscape photog.</td>', 'For me it looks muddy & the color black in the upper right dominates the image. IMO the best thing about a landscape is its abstract quality, & this one doesn''t have much abstract-for me, the best thing about this is the rocks underwater. Next time you go out to get some nice landscapes, take a moment to get a few macro shots as well. But I am not a landscape photog.', '2014-08-08 11:19:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(7249037, 1121979, 124815, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GeorgesBogaert:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mariuca:</b></div><hr/><i> I keep coming back to it (and bump) and have one thought that nags me: wouldn''t it be more powerful if you would crop the <strike>sky</strike> sea? I love the composition a lot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There is no sky on the picture, this is the sea on top. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sky or sea .... It was too late to correct it but I just had bumped it to an enthusiastic 8<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-08-08 10:25:50.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by GeorgesBogaert: Originally posted by mariuca: I keep coming back to it (and bump) and have one thought that nags me: wouldn''t it be more powerful if you would crop the sky sea? I love the composition a lot.   There is no sky on the picture, this is the sea on top.   Sky or sea .... It was too late to correct it but I just had bumped it to an enthusiastic 8', '2014-08-08 11:23:55.000000', '2014-08-08 11:25:50.000000', 0),
