(7249138, 1125689, 113591, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> probably the best ribbon in a free study in a long time. 9 from me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: probably the best ribbon in a free study in a long time. 9 from me.   Yes', '2014-08-08 14:37:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7249140, 1124384, 150277, '<td valign="top">I like the golden color captured, but those ''bumps'' in the water near the top third of the image distracted me a little, and the loon seemed a bit washed out - probably due to the pretty light - but to me - I didn''t enjoy looking at the loon as much because of the softness.</td>', 'I like the golden color captured, but those ''bumps'' in the water near the top third of the image distracted me a little, and the loon seemed a bit washed out - probably due to the pretty light - but to me - I didn''t enjoy looking at the loon as much because of the softness.', '2014-08-08 14:49:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7249141, 1125954, 113591, '<td valign="top">Such a positive vibe. Wonderful. Thanks.<br/></td>', 'Such a positive vibe. Wonderful. Thanks.', '2014-08-08 14:49:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7249153, 1125507, 77196, '<td valign="top">IMO, this is a victim of split primary subject - the rocks in the foreground, or the waterfalls? To see what I mean, look at the image with the top just above the top of the bottom water falls. <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1126809" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/77196/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1126809.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/77196/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1126809.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/77196/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1126809.jpg"/></a> <br/>This is a great shot of one falls, its catch basin and glistening rocks. Then, look at the shot with the bottom just below the white spot on the rock just left of the bottom of the falls. <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1126808" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/77196/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1126808.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/77196/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1126808.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/77196/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1126808.jpg"/></a> <br/>This is a very nice shot of a waterfalls in the woods. Either main subject is better than the shot as you entered it. <br/>Of course, you scored better than me in this challenge, so what do I know?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-08-08 14:27:48.</i></td>', 'IMO, this is a victim of split primary subject - the rocks in the foreground, or the waterfalls? To see what I mean, look at the image with the top just above the top of the bottom water falls.  This is a great shot of one falls, its catch basin and glistening rocks. Then, look at the shot with the bottom just below the white spot on the rock just left of the bottom of the falls.  This is a very nice shot of a waterfalls in the woods. Either main subject is better than the shot as you entered it. Of course, you scored better than me in this challenge, so what do I know?', '2014-08-08 15:20:09.000000', '2014-08-08 15:27:48.000000', 0),
